# ============================================================================
# Line-ending policy -- deliberately NARROW.
#
# This file pins LF for the generated-ABI surface ONLY. It is not a repo-wide
# `* text=auto` policy: that would renormalize every tracked file on the next
# checkout, which is a much larger and riskier change than the problem below.
#
# Why these files. `make check-abi` compares the two ABI facades BYTE FOR BYTE
# against the canonical constants in scripts/gen-user-abi.py (see
# CANONICAL_SHIM_* there). Those constants are Python string literals and
# therefore hold LF. A checkout made with core.autocrlf=true would hand the
# gate CRLF facades that clang compiles identically but that no longer match,
# failing every build for a difference that cannot affect which directives are
# active. check_shim_form() also normalizes newlines on read, so the two
# defenses are independent: this keeps the bytes right in the repository, that
# keeps a pre-existing clone from failing spuriously.
#
# The generated contract is listed for the same reason -- gen-user-abi.py
# renders it with LF and --check compares the rendering against the file.
# ============================================================================

abi/generated/abi_contract.h   text eol=lf
include/kernel/abi_hash.h      text eol=lf
user/include/abi_numbers.h     text eol=lf
scripts/gen-user-abi.py        text eol=lf
